Source code for running analysis

# 1 Untargeted Metabolomics (src/untargeted/)

Untargeted metabolomics processing, quality control, and statistical analysis
of human developing cortical tissue (n = 24, gestational weeks 16–24). 

# 2 Targeted Hormones (src/targeted/)
LC-MS/MS quantification of testosterone (TT), 17B-estradiol (E2), and progesterone (P4)

# 3 Gene-Hormone Analysis (src/gene-hormone/)
Pseudobulk limma-voom association of gonadal hormone concentrations with snRNA-seq gene expression across cortical cell types (n = 24, GW 16–24).
Testosterone is analyzed in males only; estradiol and progesterone are sex-combined with sex as covariate. Each hormone is tested at three annotation levels (celltype, subclass, class).

# 4 Metabolite-Gene Analyses. (src/gene-metabolite/)
Limma-voom association of untargeted metabolites with pseudobulk gene expression across cell types, followed by robustness analysis, pathway enrichment, and constraint/SFARI enrichment. 

# 5 Multi-Omics Factor Analysis (MOFA) (src/mofa)
MOFA2 integration of pseudobulk gene expression (11 cell-type views) with untargeted metabolomics (1 view, log2_na transform). Post-hoc Spearman correlation of latent factors with gonadal hormone concentrations.


